⏺ D Iwato — Japanese ritual scale. What makes it primal:

  ┌──────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │      Notes       │                  Why it's raw                   │
  ├──────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ D → D#           │ Semitone — no escape, grinding tension          │
  ├──────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ G → G#           │ Another semitone cluster — unstable, unresolved │
  ├──────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ C — the 5th note │ A tritone away from F#, never lands home        │
  └──────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  The cluster drone [D, D#, G] stacked together sounds like a koto ritual. Want to keep this as the transition and then explode back
   into something heavy, or evolve it further?

